    "title": "Drool Party kicks off at Kingsport Aquatic Center - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Faith Little ,\n9 hours ago\nKINGSPORT, Tenn. (WJHL) — The Kingsport Aquatic Center kicked off its Drool Party on Wednesday, the first of a new five-day format that will better facilitate dogs of all sizes and pet owners’ schedules.\nThe party features an open outdoor shallow pool area for dogs to splash in. Wednesday evening marked the first of five Drool Party nights, with big dogs over 25 pounds having the first chance to splash.\nBrightRidge, TVA mark 5 years of Home Uplift program The aquatic center’s Program Coordinator, Madison Gump, said this year marks the twelfth year of the party.\n“We’re just giving them another choice,” she said. “Another option to spend the evening with their dogs. A lot of dogs like to swim either at the lake or in pools. And that is what we’re doing here tonight, is just bringing the community together, providing an option for their dog friends.”\nThe remaining schedule for the 2025 Drool Party is as follows, according to Kingsport’s website:\nSept. 4; 5-7 p.m.: Small dogs only, 25 lbs or less Sept. 5; 5-7 p.m.: All dogs Sept. 6 10 a.m.-noon: All dogs 2-4 p.m.: Small dogs only, 25 lbs or less Sept. 7 10 a.m.-noon: Small dogs only, 25 lbs or less 2-4 p.m.: Big dogs only, over 25 lbs Gump said registration is open on Kingsport’s CivicRec website, and tickets can also be purchased at the door.\n“You can pre-register online at swimkingsport.com. It’s $5 for pre-registration. If you don’t know your schedule yet and need to wait, we do allow registration at the door. It’s $7 at the door per dog. Just make sure that you have that updated vaccination record with you.”\nThere is a limit of two dogs per person, and the dogs’ handlers must be over age 18. All dogs must have a leash with them, in case it’s needed.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJHL | Tri-Cities News & Weather.",
